      "previewText": "The examples below describe changes in the dispersal of matter in several processes. Fill in the blanks that correctly describe each process.Sublimation is the conversion of a solid (relatively high density) to a gas (much lower density). Because the molecules  after the solid-to-gas transition, this process  the dispersal of matter.Condensation is the conversion of a gas (relatively low density) to a liquid (much higher density). Because the molecules  after the gas-to-liquid transition, this process  the dispersal of matter.A drop of food coloring added to a glass of water forms a solution with uniform color. The food dye molecules initially occupy a  volume (the drop of dye solution) than they occupy after the process is complete (in the full glass of water). The process therefore  the dispersal of matter. ",
